{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"SUSE-SU-2026:4799-1","published":"2026-10-21T07:57:03Z","modified":"2026-10-21T20:02:15.439302894Z","related":["CVE-2026-105083","CVE-2026-106565","CVE-2026-106566","CVE-2026-106567","CVE-2026-106568","CVE-2026-106570","CVE-2026-106571","CVE-2026-106572","CVE-2026-106573","CVE-2026-106574","CVE-2026-106575","CVE-2026-106577","CVE-2026-106578","CVE-2026-106579","CVE-2026-106580","CVE-2026-107208","CVE-2026-107209","CVE-2026-107210","CVE-2026-109259","CVE-2026-109260","CVE-2026-109261","CVE-2026-109262","CVE-2026-109263","CVE-2026-109266","CVE-2026-109268","CVE-2026-109269","CVE-2026-109270","CVE-2026-109273","CVE-2026-109274","CVE-2026-109275","CVE-2026-109276","CVE-2026-109277","CVE-2026-109278","CVE-2026-93586","CVE-2026-93587","CVE-2026-93588","CVE-2026-93589"],"upstream":["CVE-2026-105083","CVE-2026-106565","CVE-2026-106566","CVE-2026-106567","CVE-2026-106568","CVE-2026-106570","CVE-2026-106571","CVE-2026-106572","CVE-2026-106573","CVE-2026-106574","CVE-2026-106575","CVE-2026-106577","CVE-2026-106578","CVE-2026-106579","CVE-2026-106580","CVE-2026-107208","CVE-2026-107209","CVE-2026-107210","CVE-2026-109259","CVE-2026-109260","CVE-2026-109261","CVE-2026-109262","CVE-2026-109263","CVE-2026-109266","CVE-2026-109268","CVE-2026-109269","CVE-2026-109270","CVE-2026-109273","CVE-2026-109274","CVE-2026-109275","CVE-2026-109276","CVE-2026-109277","CVE-2026-109278","CVE-2026-93586","CVE-2026-93587","CVE-2026-93588","CVE-2026-93589"],"summary":"Security update for ImageMagick","details":"This update for ImageMagick fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-93586: use-after-free in the `ImagesToBlob` method can lead to a process crash (bsc#1281912).\n- CVE-2026-93587: policy bypass in the PCD, CUBE and HALD coders can lead to extra memory allocation and a denial of\n  service (bsc#1281909).\n- CVE-2026-93588: NULL pointer dereference in the PNM coder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281910).\n- CVE-2026-93589: division-by-zero flaw in the FLIF encoder can lead to a denial of service (bsc#1281911).\n- CVE-2026-105083: security policy not applied when a user changes the DOCTYPE in the `policy.xml` file to something\n  else that is valid xml (bsc#1284217).\n- CVE-2026-106565: a missing end-of-file check while reading bzip2-compressed image data can cause an infinite loop\n  (bsc#1284662).\n- CVE-2026-106566: delegate symlink cleanup does not check the MAGICK_SHRED_PASSES environment variable, allowing a\n  local privileged workflow to overwrite a file with random data (bsc#1284663).\n- CVE-2026-106567: a crafted PSD file can trigger an integer-conversion error in the PSD decoder, causing an infinite\n  loop and DoS (bsc#1284664).\n- CVE-2026-106568: a crafted XMP profile embedded in an image can cause the profile parser to enter an infinite loop\n  (bsc#1284665).\n- CVE-2026-106570: an unauthenticated adjacent-network client can repeatedly connect to the distributed pixel cache\n  server and exhaust its available connections, causing a DoS (bsc#1284667).\n- CVE-2026-106571: a crafted local call to the GetVirtualPixels API can trigger an integer calculation error and write\n  beyond a heap buffer, crashing the server process (bsc#1284668).\n- CVE-2026-106572: a missing recursion-depth check in the CALS decoder allows a crafted CALS image to exhaust the call\n  stack and terminate the process (bsc#1284669).\n- CVE-2026-106573: a missing limit check in the MVG decoder allows a crafted MVG image to trigger an excessively long-\n  running operation (bsc#1284671).\n- CVE-2026-106574: a client connected to the distributed pixel cache server can send crafted pixel data that triggers a\n  heap buffer overwrite and crash the server (bsc#1284672).\n- CVE-2026-106575: a crafted Magick script can cause an opened file pointer to remain unclosed, allowing repeated\n  processing to exhaust available file descriptors (bsc#1284673).\n- CVE-2026-106577: unescaped or untrimmed values can inject code into output generated by PostScript coders\n  (bsc#1284675).\n- CVE-2026-106578: a crafted image can cause an invalid memory free in the MVG decoder and crash the process\n  (bsc#1284677).\n- CVE-2026-106579: a crafted image can bypass an ImageMagick security policy that uses coder as its domain, potentially\n  allowing data prohibited by the policy to be read (bsc#1284678).\n- CVE-2026-106580: a missing security-policy check in the CUT encoder allows a crafted local encoding operation to read\n  data that policy should deny and can also cause a crash (bsc#1284680).\n- CVE-2026-107208: a crafted XMP profile can reach a recursion limit that is handled as a fatal condition instead of an\n  ordinary exception, terminating the image-processing process (bsc#1284681).\n- CVE-2026-107209: when ImageMagick is built without Cairo support, a crafted RSVG image that reaches a resource limit\n  can cause a crash (bsc#1284682).\n- CVE-2026-107210: a crafted highly compressed MAT image can make the MAT decoder create temporary files larger than the\n  configured security-policy limit (bsc#1284683).\n- CVE-2026-109259: Information disclosure via crafted TGA image (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109260: Denial of Service via memory leak in PNG encoder (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109261: Denial of Service via memory leak in GIF encoder (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109262: Denial of Service via memory leak in SVG encoder (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109263: Denial of Service via memory leak in YUV encoder (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109266: XML injection vulnerability in the CIP encoder (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109268: Denial of Service via use-after-free in PDF writer (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109269: Information disclosure via crafted JPEG file (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109270: Denial of Service via memory leak in the -process option (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109273: Information disclosure via crafted PostScript file (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109275: Code injection via crafted MVG file (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109276: Denial of Service via temporary file leak in JNG decoder (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109277: Security policy bypass via -script operation (bsc#1285071).\n- CVE-2026-109278: Denial of Service via memory leak in wavelet-denoise operation (bsc#1285071).\n","affected":[{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise Module for Desktop Applications 15 SP7","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/ImageMagick&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20Module%20for%20Desktop%20Applications%2015%20SP7"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"ImageMagick-config-7-upstream":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4799-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-ESPOS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/ImageMagick&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-ESPOS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"binaries":[{"ImageMagick":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","ImageMagick-config-7-SUSE":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","ImageMagick-config-7-upstream":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","ImageMagick-devel":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","libMagick++-7_Q16HDRI5":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","libMagick++-devel":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","libMagickCore-7_Q16HDRI10":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","libMagickWand-7_Q16HDRI10":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1","perl-PerlMagick":"7.1.0.9-150400.6.122.1"}]},"database_specific":{"source":"https://ftp.suse.com/pub/projects/security/osv/SUSE-SU-2026:4799-1.json"}},{"package":{"name":"ImageMagick","ecosystem":"SUSE:Linux Enterprise High Performance Computing 15 SP4-LTSS","purl":"pkg:rpm/suse/ImageMagick&distro=SUSE%20Linux%20Enterprise%20High%20Performance%20Computing%2015%20SP4-LTSS"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed"